// The questions founders actually ask, with the answers we actually give.
// The free-text box matches on these keywords before falling back to "ask us".
const qa = [
	{
		q: 'How much does it cost?',
		k: ['cost', 'price', 'budget', 'much', 'pay', 'fee', 'quote', 'expensive', 'naira', 'dollar'],
		a: 'It is scoped, not guessed. We run a short discovery, agree exactly what is being built, then quote a fixed price for that scope, so the number you get is the number you pay. Smaller builds start modestly; a full marketplace is a different conversation. Tell us the idea and you get a real figure within a business day.',
	},
	{
		q: 'How long until I launch?',
		k: ['long', 'time', 'week', 'fast', 'quick', 'deadline', 'when', 'launch', 'timeline'],
		a: 'Six weeks is our usual ceiling for a first release, not a floor. A booking site or a landing product often goes live in two to three; a marketplace or an ERP takes longer. We tell you which one you are on day one, in writing, and you watch the build every week.',
	},
	{
		q: 'Who owns the code?',
		k: ['own', 'code', 'repo', 'ip', 'rights', 'source', 'licence', 'license'],
		a: 'You do. Every repository, domain, account and design file is yours, handed over documented at launch. We do not hold your product hostage, and you are free to take it to any other team whenever you like.',
	},
	{
		q: 'Can you take over an existing product?',
		k: ['existing', 'take over', 'takeover', 'inherit', 'already', 'built', 'rescue', 'legacy', 'fix', 'another'],
		a: 'Often, yes. We start with a paid audit of what you have, covering the code, the infrastructure and the risks, then give you an honest call: stabilise it, extend it, or rebuild the parts that are costing you. Plenty of our long-running clients came to us this way.',
	},
	{
		q: 'Do you work outside Nigeria?',
		k: ['nigeria', 'outside', 'abroad', 'country', 'international', 'remote', 'global', 'timezone', 'us', 'uk'],
		a: 'Yes. We are based in Abuja and our work runs in 10+ countries. We work in your hours for the meetings that matter, and everything else happens on a board you can see any time you like.',
	},
	{
		q: 'What happens after launch?',
		k: ['after', 'launch', 'support', 'maintain', 'maintenance', 'grow', 'marketing', 'scale', 'stay'],
		a: 'We stay. Hosting, monitoring, backups and same-day fixes as standard. If you want it, our marketing team keeps growing the thing we just built. Ask about AnchorStep: we built the site and the booking system, then ran the social account too.',
		go: '#fd-spotlight',
		goT: 'See what that looks like',
	},
	{
		q: 'Who is the CEO?',
		k: ['ceo', 'founder', 'owner', 'boss', 'who runs', 'who started', 'tosky', 'tochukwu', 'nnamdi', 'nwaeze', 'management', 'leader', 'director'],
		a: 'Swizel is led by Engr. Tochukwu Nnamdi-Nwaeze, Tosky, who founded the company in 2019 while still at university and still sits in on builds. His note to founders is further down this page, signed, with his LinkedIn under it.',
		go: '#fd-founder',
		goT: 'Read his note',
	},
	{
		q: 'What do you actually build?',
		k: ['what do you', 'what you do', 'services', 'build', 'offer', 'capabilit', 'website', 'app', 'software', 'erp', 'ecommerce'],
		a: 'Websites and web apps, iOS and Android, e-commerce and marketplaces, brand and design, APIs and integrations, teams as a service, and the hosting and support that keeps all of it running. Every slide in this deck is one of those, with a live Swizel product behind it.',
		go: '#fd-deck',
		goT: 'See the deck',
	},
	{
		q: 'Can I see your work?',
		k: ['work', 'portfolio', 'case study', 'projects', 'examples', 'built before', 'clients', 'proof', 'receipts'],
		a: '65+ products are live across 10+ countries: marketplaces, betting tools, media platforms, booking systems. The wall further down this page opens each one, and the portfolio has the full set with what we did and what it moved.',
		go: '/portfolio',
		goT: 'Open the portfolio',
	},
	{
		q: 'How big is the team?',
		k: ['team', 'big', 'many people', 'staff', 'size', 'who works', 'engineers', 'bench', 'specialists'],
		a: '25+ specialists on the bench: engineering, design, product and delivery, plus a marketing team that takes over after launch. You get a named senior lead, not a rotating pool, and you meet the people who will actually write your code.',
		go: '/about#team',
		goT: 'Meet the crew',
	},
	{
		q: 'How do we start?',
		k: ['start', 'begin', 'get going', 'first step', 'next step', 'onboard', 'kick off', 'hire you', 'work with you', 'contact'],
		a: 'One call. You tell us the idea, we tell you honestly whether it is two weeks or twelve, then you get a fixed scope and a fixed price in writing. Week one is discovery and design; you see something clickable by the end of it.',
		go: '/contact',
		goT: 'Start a project',
	},
	{
		q: 'Do you do branding and design?',
		k: ['brand', 'design', 'logo', 'identity', 'ui', 'ux', 'visual', 'creative', 'content'],
		a: 'Yes. Identity, design systems, product UI, and the content that goes with it. AnchorStep is the clearest example: we built her site and booking system, then did the brand and now run the social account too.',
		go: '#fd-spotlight',
		goT: 'See the spotlight',
	},
	{
		q: 'Do you train people?',
		k: ['train', 'intern', 'internship', 'academy', 'campus', 'learn', 'student', 'mentor', 'programme', 'program', 'graduate'],
		a: 'We do. Swizel Campus takes people into the same Abuja floor the client work happens on, on live builds with senior review, not toy projects. Two ways in, and both end with something shipped and in your name.',
		go: '/programs',
		goT: 'See the programmes',
	},
	{
		q: 'How do payments work?',
		k: ['payment', 'milestone', 'instal', 'deposit', 'upfront', 'invoice', 'terms', 'nda', 'contract', 'agreement'],
		a: 'Fixed scope, fixed price, paid against milestones you sign off, never one lump sum in advance. Contracts and NDAs are normal here; we sign yours or send ours, whichever is faster for your side.',
	},
	{
		q: 'Where are you based?',
		k: ['based', 'located', 'office', 'address', 'abuja', 'where are you'],
		a: 'Abuja, Nigeria. A real floor with a real team on it, which you are welcome to visit. The work runs in 10+ countries from there, in your hours for the meetings that matter.',
		go: '/contact',
		goT: 'Find us',
	},
];

// The same questions, handed to search engines as an FAQ. Google reads the
// answers here word for word, so this block is generated from the rail above
// rather than written twice: the page and the schema can never drift apart.
const faqSchema = {
	'@context': 'https://schema.org',
	'@type': 'FAQPage',
	mainEntity: qa.map((item) => ({
		'@type': 'Question',
		name: item.q,
		acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: item.a },
	})),
};
---

<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} is:inline />

<section class="pdeck-sec" id="fd-deck" data-cursor="repo">
	<span class="pdeck-ground" aria-hidden="true"></span>

	<div class="pdeck-wrap">
		<div class="pdeck-head fd-rev">
			<span class="pdeck-stamp">
				<Icon class="pdeck-stamp-ic" width={13} name="mdi:filmstrip" />
				Now showing
			</span>
			<h2 class="pdeck-h">What we <em>actually do.</em></h2>
		</div>

		<div class="pdeck fd-rev" id="pdeck" data-pdeck style={`--pd-acc:${slides[0].accent}`}>
			<!-- the house: two beams that sweep the wall behind everything -->
			<span class="pdeck__house" aria-hidden="true">
				<span class="pdeck__beam pdeck__beam--l"></span>
				<span class="pdeck__beam pdeck__beam--r"></span>
				<span class="pdeck__dust"></span>
			</span>

			<!-- the clicker rail -->
			<div class="pdeck__rail">
				<span class="pdeck__count">
					<b data-pd-now>01</b><i>/</i><span>{String(slides.length).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
				</span>

				<div class="pdeck__dots" role="tablist" aria-label="Slides">
					{
						slides.map((s, i) => (
							<button
								class="pdeck__dot"
								type="button"
								role="tab"
								data-pd-dot={i}
								aria-selected={i === 0 ? 'true' : 'false'}
								aria-label={`${s.kicker}, slide ${i + 1}`}
								style={`--d:${s.accent}`}
							>
								<span class="pdeck__dot-tip">{s.kicker}</span>
							</button>
						))
					}
				</div>

				<div class="pdeck__tools">
					<button class="pdeck__tool" type="button" data-pd-play aria-label="Play the deck">
						<Icon class="pdeck__i-play" width={15} name="mdi:play" />
						<Icon class="pdeck__i-stop" width={15} name="mdi:pause" />
						<span class="pdeck__tool-t">Play</span>
					</button>
					<button class="pdeck__tool pdeck__tool--lights" type="button" data-pd-lights aria-pressed="false">
						<Icon class="pdeck__i-off" width={15} name="mdi:lightbulb-outline" />
						<Icon class="pdeck__i-on" width={15} name="mdi:lightbulb-on-outline" />
						<span class="pdeck__tool-t" data-pd-lights-t>Kill the lights</span>
					</button>
				</div>
			</div>

			<span class="pdeck__prog" aria-hidden="true"><span data-pd-prog></span></span>

			<!-- the stage -->
			<div class="pdeck__stage" data-pd-stage tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Pitch deck">
				{
					slides.map((s, i) => (
						<article
							class="pdeck__slide"
							data-pd-slide={i}
							style={`--pd-a:${s.accent}; --pd-b:${s.accent2}`}
							aria-hidden={i === 0 ? 'false' : 'true'}
						>
							<span class="pdeck__wash" aria-hidden="true" />

							<div class="pdeck__copy">
								<span class="pdeck__kick">
									<Icon width={14} name={s.kickerIcon} />
									{s.kicker}
									<i class="pdeck__kick-rule" aria-hidden="true" />
								</span>
								<h3 class="pdeck__t">
									{s.title} <em>{s.em}</em>
								</h3>
								<p class="pdeck__line">{s.line}</p>

								<!-- four notes, the way a founder writes them down -->
								<ul class="pdeck__stickies">
									{s.notes.map((nt, k) => (
										<li style={`--k:${k}`}>
											<b>{nt.t}</b>
											<em>{nt.d}</em>
										</li>
									))}
								</ul>

								<ul class="pdeck__figs">
									{figures.map((f) => (
										<li>
											<span class="pdeck__fig-ic"><Icon width={15} name={f.icon} /></span>
											<b>{f.v}</b>
											<em>{f.l}</em>
										</li>
									))}
								</ul>
							</div>

							<div class="pdeck__show">
								<span class="pdeck__glow" aria-hidden="true" />

								<div class="pdeck__rig">
									<span class="pdeck__lap">
										<span class="pdeck__lap-screen">
											<img
												src={s.work.img}
												alt={`${s.work.name}, built by Swizel`}
												loading={i === 0 ? 'eager' : 'lazy'}
												decoding="async"
												width="1280"
												height="800"
											/>
											<span class="pdeck__glare" aria-hidden="true" />
										</span>
										<span class="pdeck__lap-base" aria-hidden="true" />
									</span>

									<span class="pdeck__phone" aria-hidden="true">
										<span class="pdeck__phone-screen">
											<img src={s.work.img} alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
										</span>
									</span>

									{s.marks.map((nt, k) => (
										<span class={`pdeck__mark pdeck__mark--${k + 1}`} style={`--t:${nt.tint}; --k:${k}`}>
											<span class="pdeck__mark-ic"><Icon width={15} name={nt.icon} /></span>
											<span class="pdeck__mark-txt">
												<b>{nt.title}</b>
												<em>{nt.body}</em>
											</span>
										</span>
									))}
								</div>

								<a
									class="pdeck__work"
									href={s.work.url}
									target={s.work.url.startsWith('http') ? '_blank' : undefined}
									rel={s.work.url.startsWith('http') ? 'noopener' : undefined}
								>
									<span class="pdeck__work-mark" aria-hidden="true">
										<Icon width={19} name={s.kickerIcon} />
									</span>
									<span class="pdeck__work-txt">
										<strong>{s.work.name}</strong>
										<span class="pdeck__sector">{s.work.sector}</span>
										<span class="pdeck__note-line">{s.work.note}</span>
									</span>
									<span class="pdeck__work-go" aria-hidden="true">
										<Icon width={17} name="mdi:arrow-right" />
									</span>
								</a>
							</div>
						</article>
					))
				}

				<!-- the projected answer, over whichever slide is up -->
				<div class="pdeck__answer" data-pd-answer hidden>
					<span class="pdeck__answer-beam" aria-hidden="true"></span>
					<div class="pdeck__answer-card">
						<span class="pdeck__answer-k">
							<Icon width={14} name="mdi:comment-question-outline" />
							You asked
						</span>
						<h4 data-pd-answer-q>…</h4>
						<p data-pd-answer-a>…</p>
						<div class="pdeck__answer-row">
							<a class="pdeck__answer-cta" data-pd-answer-go hidden href="#">
								<span data-pd-answer-go-t>Take me there</span>
								<Icon width={15} name="mdi:arrow-down-right" />
							</a>
							<a href="/contact" class="pdeck__answer-cta pdeck__answer-cta--ghost" data-pd-answer-ask>
								Ask us properly
								<Icon width={15} name="mdi:arrow-right" />
							</a>
							<button type="button" class="pdeck__answer-x" data-pd-answer-close>
								Back to the deck
							</button>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>

				<button class="pdeck__nav pdeck__nav--prev" type="button" data-pd-prev aria-label="Previous slide">
					<Icon width={20} name="mdi:chevron-left" />
				</button>
				<button class="pdeck__nav pdeck__nav--next" type="button" data-pd-next aria-label="Next slide">
					<Icon width={20} name="mdi:chevron-right" />
				</button>
			</div>

			<!-- ── the Q&A rail ─────────────────────────────────────── -->
			<div class="pdeck__qa">
				<span class="pdeck__qa-k">
					<Icon width={15} name="mdi:hand-back-left-outline" />
					Questions from the floor
				</span>
				<div class="pdeck__qa-chips" data-pd-chips>
					{
						qa.slice(0, 6).map((item, i) => (
							<button class="pdeck__qa-chip" type="button" data-pd-ask={i}>
								{item.q}
							</button>
						))
					}
				</div>
				<form class="pdeck__qa-form" data-pd-qa-form>
					<Icon class="pdeck__qa-ic" width={16} name="mdi:magnify" />
					<input
						type="text"
						data-pd-qa-input
						placeholder="…or type your own question"
						aria-label="Ask the deck a question"
						autocomplete="off"
					/>
					<button type="submit" aria-label="Ask">
						<Icon width={16} name="mdi:send" />
					</button>
				</form>
			</div>

			<!-- ── the curtain, closed until you raise it ───────────── -->
			<div class="pdeck__curtain" data-pd-curtain>
				<span class="pdeck__velvet pdeck__velvet--l" aria-hidden="true"></span>
				<span class="pdeck__velvet pdeck__velvet--r" aria-hidden="true"></span>
				<span class="pdeck__pelmet" aria-hidden="true"></span>
				<div class="pdeck__marquee">
					<span class="pdeck__marquee-k">
						<Icon class="pdeck__marquee-ic" width={13} name="mdi:movie-open-outline" />
						Swizel presents
					</span>
					<h3 class="pdeck__marquee-h">The&nbsp;services <em>pitch&nbsp;deck</em></h3>
					<p class="pdeck__marquee-p">
						Seven disciplines. Seven live products. About ninety seconds.
					</p>
					<button class="pdeck__marquee-go" type="button" data-pd-open>
						<Icon width={17} name="mdi:movie-open-play-outline" />
						Raise the curtain
					</button>
					<span class="pdeck__marquee-s">or it opens by itself in a moment</span>
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- the answers, handed to the clicker script -->
			<script type="application/json" data-pd-qa set:html={JSON.stringify(qa)}></script>

			<button class="pdeck__exit" type="button" data-pd-exit aria-label="Leave the presentation">
				<span class="pdeck__exit-x" aria-hidden="true">
					<Icon width={17} name="mdi:close" />
				</span>
				<span class="pdeck__exit-t">Close<kbd>Esc</kbd></span>
			</button>
			<span class="pdeck__hint">← → to move · Esc to leave</span>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<div class="pdeck-blackout" data-pd-blackout hidden></div>

<style>
	/* ══ the auditorium ══ */
	.pdeck-sec {
